  "Influence of the Reserve:\nServices, Ind. and SoL: +": "储备影响：\n服务/工业/民生：+",
  "Influence of the Reserve:\nServices, Ind. and SoL: +0.": "储备影响：\n服务/工业/民生：+0.",
  "Influence of the Reserve:\nServices, Ind. and SoL: -": "储备影响：\n服务/工业/民生：-",
  "Influence of the Reserve:\nServices, Ind. and SoL: -0.": "储备影响：\n服务/工业/民生：-0.",
  "\nCorruption -0.": "\n腐败 -0.",
  "\nYour alliance stability +": "\n同盟稳定性 +",
  "|Inspired by the success of the Chinese automation, Romanov decided to start mass implementation of automation planning, and continued development of the CSA and USNCC, and, taking from a shelf project OGAS, development and implementation of which managed to finish, despite dissatisfaction with the party members. Romanov led the Soviet Union until his death in 2008, during which time repeatedly raising the international influence of the USSR, its economic power and the welfare of the population.": "|受中国自动化成功的鼓舞，罗曼诺夫决定大规模推行自动化计划，并继续开发自动化控制系统（CSA）与全国计算中心联网系统（USNCC）；同时从搁置项目全国自动化管理系统入手，其开发与实施最终得以完成，尽管党内成员颇有不满。罗曼诺夫一直领导苏联到2008年去世，在此期间反复提升苏联的国际影响力、经济实力与民众福利。",
  "|Having seen by personal example the failure of the results of the economic policy of Hungary and Yugoslavia, Romanov decided to take a different path from Andropov's plans and to start mass implementation of automation planning. He continued development of the CSA and USNCC, and, taking from a shelf project OGAS, development and implementation of which managed to finish, despite dissatisfaction with the party members. Romanov led the Soviet Union until his death in 2008, during which time repeatedly raising the international influence of the USSR, its economic power and the welfare of the population.": "|亲眼见证匈牙利与南斯拉夫经济政策的结果失败后，罗曼诺夫决定走与安德罗波夫计划不同的道路，开始大规模推行自动化计划。他继续开发自动化控制系统（CSA）与全国计算中心联网系统（USNCC），并从搁置项目全国自动化管理系统入手，其开发与实施最终得以完成，尽管党内成员不满。罗曼诺夫一直领导苏联到2008年去世，在此期间反复提升苏联的国际影响力、经济实力与民众福利。",
  "Comrade Chairman! New news from Turkey! On September 12, <color=#2F4F4F>The National Security Council</color> announced a coup d'état on national television. The NSS headed by Chief of General Staff <color=#2F4F4F>K. Evren</color> dissolved the parliament, removed the government of S. Demirel from power, banned strikes and trade unions, suspended the activities of most political parties. and Ataturk's reforms. The document declared the readiness of the new government to be faithful to all treaties and alliances of Turkey, including NATO.{0}A flurry of repressions fell upon all parliamentary organizations.{0}In the current situation, we can consider the following measures.": "主席同志，土耳其传来新消息！9月12日，<color=#2F4F4F>国家安全委员会</color>通过全国电视宣布发动政变。由总参谋长<color=#2F4F4F>凯南·埃夫伦</color>领导的委员会解散议会，撤销苏莱曼·德米雷尔政府，禁止罢工和工会活动，并暂停大多数政党的活动，宣称维护阿塔图尔克的改革。声明还宣布，新政府将履行土耳其参加的所有条约和联盟，包括北约。{0}一轮镇压席卷了所有议会组织。{0}在当前局势下，我们可以考虑采取以下措施。",
  "When Konrad Naumann came to power, he was concerned with \"returning the party to its popular roots\" and combating the \"detachment of party functionaries\". The right of voters to recall deputies was introduced, the right of workers' collectives to dismiss directors was introduced, electronic reception centres for the Presidency administration were organised, and party members themselves were obliged to travel exclusively by public transport and to hold all meetings openly and live. Nauman himself was not afraid of such changes, being a straightforward man who easily found common ground with ordinary workers and rank-and-file party members, organising parties and drinks with them. This closeness to the people he would try to instil in the entire SED in the future.| In cultural policy Naumann announced a New Cultural Revolution, but not along the lines of Mao, but along the \"lines of Lenin\": travel to the capitals (and to the FRG) was completely banned, party workers and artists were now only allowed to travel to socialist countries; the re-promotion of the \"Soviet avant-garde\" and the fight against \"bourgeois art\" began, and attacks on postmodernist art and Western modernism were launched. Along with this, rock, rap, punk and meth were allowed, but only in the form of \"socialist meaning.\" During one of his speeches, Nauman even declared that \"at least the majority of artists and writers are essentially idiots\", after which mass dismissals took place across the ranks of the art councils and new young talents took their places.|In economics, Nauman was faced with a huge foreign debt and \"an economic policy that contradicted the interests of the workers and the decisions of the Eighth Party Congress of 1971\". To meet this challenge, the OSNP (the state trade union) was given a voice in the formation of the five-year plan, its official representatives became mandatory participants in Politburo meetings at the national level, lower-level representatives became participants in local party meetings with voting rights, and labour collectives were given a similar voice among their enterprises and local planning bodies. In this way workers were able to participate and intervene in the work of the planning committee, party meetings and enterprises.It cannot be said that this radically changed the situation in the country because of the passivity of the population and the bureaucratisation of the organs, but the simple and charismatic \"Connie\", from all corners of the newspapers, radio and television, began to urge the people to use their opportunities and \"show the bureaucracy and the idle economists their place\", so that the masses of the people gradually began to use their new opportunities and rights, and t h e y began to take advantage of their new opportunities and rights. The renewal of East Germany from the grassroots (while maintaining the one-party planned economy) has begun!": "当康拉德·瑙曼上台时，他关心的是“让党回到群众根基”，并打击“党务干部脱离群众”。引入了选民召回议员的权利；引入了工人集体解雇董事的权利；为总统府行政部门组织了电子接待中心；并要求党员自己只能乘坐公共交通工具出行，且所有会议都必须公开举行并现场参与。瑙曼本人并不害怕这些变化——他是个直来直去的人，很容易与普通工人和基层党成员找到共同点，组织聚会与饮酒活动。通过这种亲民方式，他将来会把这种做法灌输到整个德国统一社会党。| 在文化政策上，瑙曼宣布“新的文化革命”，但并非沿着毛的路线，而是沿着“列宁的路线”：前往首都（以及联邦德国）被彻底禁止；党务人员与艺术家只能前往社会主义国家；重新大力宣传“苏联先锋派”，并开始打击“资产阶级艺术”；同时发动对后现代主义艺术与西方现代主义的攻击。与此同时，摇滚、说唱、朋克和金属乐也被允许，但只能以“社会主义意义”的形式出现。在一次演讲中，瑙曼甚至宣称“至少大多数艺术家和作家本质上都是白痴”，随后艺术委员会各层级出现大规模撤换，新的年轻人才顶上。| 在经济方面，瑙曼面对巨额外债以及“违背工人利益、并背离1971年八大党代会决议的经济政策”。为应对这一挑战，自由德国工会联合会（国家贸易工会）在制定五年计划时获得发言权；其官方代表成为全国层面政治局会议的强制参与者；基层代表则成为地方党会议的有表决权参与者；而劳动集体也在其企业与地方规划机构中获得类似的发言权。这样，工人就能参与并介入计划委员会、党会议与企业的工作。不得不说，这并没有因为民众的被动与机关官僚化而彻底改变局势，但报纸、广播与电视各处那位简单且富有魅力的“康妮”（康尼）开始敦促民众利用自己的机会，“让官僚和懒散的经济学家知道自己的位置”，于是群众逐渐开始使用新的机会与权利，并开始利用这些权利。自下而上（同时维持一党制计划经济）的东德更新已经开始了！",
  "Comrade Chairman! New news from Turkey! On September 12, The National Security Council announced a coup d'état on national television. The NSS headed by Chief of General Staff K. Evren dissolved the parliament, removed the government of S. Demirel from power, banned strikes and trade unions, suspended the activities of most political parties. and Ataturk's reforms. The document declared the readiness of the new government to be faithful to all treaties and alliances of Turkey, including NATO.{0}A flurry of repressions fell upon all parliamentary organizations.{0}In the current situation, we can consider the following measures.": "主席同志，土耳其传来新消息！9月12日，国家安全委员会通过全国电视宣布发动政变。由总参谋长凯南·埃夫伦领导的委员会解散议会，撤销苏莱曼·德米雷尔政府，禁止罢工和工会活动，并暂停大多数政党的活动，宣称维护阿塔图尔克的改革。声明还宣布，新政府将履行土耳其参加的所有条约和联盟，包括北约。{0}一轮镇压席卷了所有议会组织。{0}在当前局势下，我们可以考虑采取以下措施。"
}